          "page": 6,
          "section": "Discussion",
          "quote": "The amount of FCC fraction reduction in 700 °C/5 h sample is almost doubled compared to 700 °C/1 h sample during tensile deformation, hence the more significance of FCC to BCC TRIP in 700 °C/5 h sample is the reason for the more obvious hump observed in the strain hardening rate curve as shown in Fig. 3 b, and more severe TRIP effect could also be the reason why 700 °C/5 h sample presents larger total elongation than that of 700 °C/1 h sample.",
